course: dictionary
lesson: 14478
title: A word for a church leader
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pastor is a church leader. A pastor leads a church and looks after the people who go there, the way a shepherd looks after sheep. Context helps: «Pastor John prayed with the family after the funeral.» Praying with people and comforting them are clues that a pastor is a church leader.
explain: Often a church leader is called by the title «Pastor» before a name, like «Pastor Smith». Look for the capital P and the name after it. «The youth pastor runs the games night on Fridays.» The word youth tells you this pastor works mainly with young people at the church.
explain: Pastor can also be a verb, but this is rare. «She was asked to pastor the small church by the river.» Here pastor means to be the pastor of a church. It is an action word, so you can tell it is used as a verb because of the words around it.
fact: A pastor is a Christian minister who leads a church and cares for its people.
fact: The word pastor comes from a Latin word meaning «shepherd».
fact: A shepherd looks after sheep, and a pastor looks after people in a similar caring way.
fact: Pastor is used as a title in many churches, especially Protestant churches, such as «Pastor Lee».
fact: «Youth pastor» means a pastor who works mainly with young people.
exercise: «Pastor Lee gave a talk at church on Sunday.» What is a pastor? | *A church leader who cares for the people | A person who sells food at the market | A type of sheep | A teacher who works only at school
exercise: «The pastor visited Mrs Brown when she was ill.» What is the pastor doing? | Painting the church roof | Selling tickets | *Caring for a church member | Driving a bus
exercise: Why is the word pastor linked to shepherds? | Because shepherds sing in church | *Because a pastor looks after people like a shepherd looks after sheep | Because shepherds and pastors both live in cities
test: «Youth pastor Sam runs games for teenagers.» What does youth pastor mean? | *A pastor who works mainly with young people | A baker who makes bread for the church | A sheep farmer | A player in the youth football team
test: In «She was asked to pastor the small church», what kind of word is pastor? | A preposition, a place word | An adjective, a describing word | *A verb, an action word, used rarely | A noun, a name for a person
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to pastor as a church leader? | Baker | Teacher | Farmer | *Minister
